From 87d0aee43a273fee5c8171c7492957e6b52131a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Thu, 14 May 2026 12:00:10 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] perf phase 11 patch 0142 -- wave-47 OPL3 reg 0xBD chip-wide
 latch clear

Per flush-instr's docs/internal/WAVE-46-LOG-ANALYSIS.md hypothesis H6
(60-70% probability fit; 30-40% remaining uncertainty assigned to H1
envelope tail / H5 placeholder write garbage): operator wave-46 real-
HW listening reports the "wub-wub" post-quit artifact PERSISTS despite
patch SDL/0059 DSP RESET firing correctly. The DSP RESET silences the
SB16 DAC residual but the wub-wub is upstream of the DAC mix.

H6 root cause: OPL3 register 0xBD is a chip-wide tremolo/vibrato/
percussion-mode latch. Bit 7 = 4.8 dB tremolo depth at ~3.7 Hz --
exact match to the operator-reported audible cadence. The latch is
NOT cleared by per-voice SDL_DOSOpl3VoiceNoteOff (which writes only
the per-voice KEY-ON/freq registers 0xA0/0xB0). Once set (potentially
by accidental writes during MIDI dispatch from the 8-patch placeholder
bank or buggy program-change events; the SDL OPL3 init in
vendor/SDL/src/core/dos/SDL_dos_audio_synth.c does NOT write to
0xBD), it survives KEY-OFF-all + SDL_DOSOpl3Shutdown and continues
modulating any residual analog output until explicit clear or chip
power-down.

Fix: single SDL_DOSOpl3WriteRegister(0xBD, 0x00) call in
MidiBackendOpl3::~MidiBackendOpl3() inserted BEFORE the existing
KEY-OFF-all loop. Order matters per team-lead's directive: clear
chip-wide latches FIRST so subsequent KEY-OFF writes can't race with
a tremolo-modulated output tail.

Implementation note: team-lead's brief used raw outportb() (2 lines:
outportb(0x388, 0xBD); outportb(0x389, 0x00);). Authored via the
existing SDL_DOSOpl3WriteRegister helper instead (1 line). The
helper routes ports correctly (primary bank 0x388/0x389 vs secondary
0x38A/0x38B for regs >= 0x100; 0xBD is primary-bank) AND handles the
YMF262-mandated ~6-us inter-write delay via the canonical Adlib
6-dummy-status-read pattern (per
vendor/SDL/src/core/dos/SDL_dos_audio_synth.c:416). Raw outportb
would skip those delays + risk timing-related glitches on the
14.318 MHz YMF262 on PODP83 ISA bus. The helper is already declared
extern in MidiBackendOpl3.cpp line 62 and used elsewhere in the
file -- this is the right abstraction layer.

Killswitch: NONE. Clearing the latch is safe under all OPL3
configurations:
- If latch was set (H6 hypothesis correct): wub-wub fix engages.
- If latch was NOT set (H6 hypothesis wrong): write is a no-op.
- The clear cannot REGRESS anything -- it can only fix or no-op.

Per [[no_playing_it_safe]] + flush-instr's H6 probability ranking,
ship default-ON. If wave-47 operator listening still reports
wub-wub, H6 is falsified and the next investigative step is
probe-engineer's opl3safe.c probe per flush-instr's 17-step
ear-test matrix in WAVE-46-LOG-ANALYSIS.md sec. 7.1.

Banner: "opl3 backend: cleared reg 0xBD chip-wide latch (wub-wub
mitigation per flush-instr WAVE-46 H6)" -- emitted at clear time
inside the shutdown path. Optional severity in
tests/run-gameplay-smoke.sh BANNERS (mirrors patch SDL/0059 emit
pattern: fires on clean exit only; DOSBox-X smoke pkill-on-timeout
won't emit and that's not a failure).

Ride-along discipline: this is a pure correctness fix on the wave-47
binary. The wave-47 perf lever is mds_tilemap_bg sub-decomp (flush-
instr designing in parallel). Per [[single_lever_per_binary]]: ONE
new perf mechanism per binary, correctness ride-alongs are free.
---
 src/sound/MidiBackendOpl3.cpp | 35 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 35 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/sound/MidiBackendOpl3.cpp b/src/sound/MidiBackendOpl3.cpp
index 77b662b..1923cd4 100644
--- a/src/sound/MidiBackendOpl3.cpp
+++ b/src/sound/MidiBackendOpl3.cpp
@@ -527,6 +527,41 @@ MidiBackendOpl3::~MidiBackendOpl3()
     // had `if (_voices[v].active)` guard which skipped voices whose
     // engine-side active=false but had chip KEY-ON=1 (drift). The
     // guard is now removed; all 18 voices KEY-OFF unconditionally.
+    //
+    // patch 0142 (wave-47 wub-wub mitigation): clear OPL3 register
+    // 0xBD chip-wide tremolo/vibrato/percussion latch BEFORE the
+    // KEY-OFF-all loop. Per flush-instr's WAVE-46-LOG-ANALYSIS.md
+    // hypothesis H6 (60-70% probability fit on operator's reported
+    // post-quit "wub-wub" artifact): reg 0xBD bit 7 = 4.8 dB tremolo
+    // depth at ~3.7 Hz, which exactly matches the operator's audible
+    // cadence. The 0xBD latch is chip-wide (not per-voice) and is
+    // NOT cleared by SDL_DOSOpl3VoiceNoteOff (which only writes the
+    // per-voice KEY-ON/freq registers 0xA0/0xB0). Once set
+    // (potentially by accidental writes during MIDI dispatch from
+    // the 8-patch placeholder bank or buggy program-change events),
+    // it survives the KEY-OFF-all + SDL_DOSOpl3Shutdown sequence and
+    // continues to modulate any residual analog output until explicit
+    // clear or chip power-down (the operator-reported behavior).
+    //
+    // Order: clear the chip-wide latch FIRST so subsequent KEY-OFF
+    // writes can't accidentally race with a tremolo-modulated output
+    // tail. The clear is a 2-byte write (reg-select + 0x00 data)
+    // routed through SDL_DOSOpl3WriteRegister, which handles the
+    // YMF262-mandated ~6-us inter-write delay (canonical Adlib
+    // 6-dummy-status-read pattern) -- doing this via raw outportb
+    // would skip those delays + risk timing-related glitches on a
+    // 14.318 MHz YMF262 on PODP83 ISA bus.
+    //
+    // Killswitch: none. Clearing the latch is safe under all OPL3
+    // configurations; if the latch wasn't set this is a no-op, and
+    // if it was set this is exactly the wub-wub fix. Per [[no_
+    // playing_it_safe]] this ships default-ON. If wave-47 operator
+    // listening still reports wub-wub, H6 is falsified and the next
+    // step is probe-engineer's opl3safe.c (flush-instr's 17-step
+    // ear-test matrix in WAVE-46-LOG-ANALYSIS.md sec. 7.1).
+    SDL_DOSOpl3WriteRegister(0xBD, 0x00);
+    LOG_INFO("opl3 backend: cleared reg 0xBD chip-wide latch "
+             "(wub-wub mitigation per flush-instr WAVE-46 H6)");
     for (int v = 0; v < VOICES; ++v)
     {
       SDL_DOSOpl3VoiceNoteOff(v);
-- 
